    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as defined by `owners.POST.yml` and the function classes it wires together. I've marked each item as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state, persists, logs, or computes output).\n\n## Before the pipeline\n\n- **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` guards the whole endpoint. A caller without that role never enters the pipeline (\u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## Pipeline steps (in order)\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency**\n   - [side-effect] Publishes the `Idempotency-Key` request header into a pipeline variable (for step 16).\n   - [validation] If that key was already used to create an owner, short-circuits with `IdempotentReplayException` (replays the prior owner id instead of creating a duplicate).\n\n2. **RequireOwnerFields**\n   - [side-effect] `StructuredAddress.apply` \u2014 normalises the address; if `addressLine1` is supplied it normalises line1/line2 and composes the flat `address` from them, otherwise normalises the flat `address`.\n   - [validation] `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must all be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n   - [side-effect] Normalises `telephone` to E.164 form (`E164Telephone`); [validation] if no valid E.164 number can be formed \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")`.\n   - [side-effect] Republishes the (now-mutated) body as a variable for later steps.\n\n3. **RequireCurrentRegistrationDate**\n   - [validation] If `registrationDate` is supplied it must not be after today's server date \u2192 else `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent is allowed.\n\n4. **RequirePostcode**\n   - [validation] If `postcode` is supplied it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region it must fall in range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent is allowed.\n\n5. **NormaliseEmail**\n   - [validation] If `email` is supplied it must be syntactically valid and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"email\")`.\n   - [side-effect] Lower-cases the email in place. Absent is allowed.\n\n> **Transaction begins here** \u2014 every step from 6 through 13 carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads/writes commit once at the end of the pipeline.\n\n6. **RequireUniqueIdentity** *(txn)*\n   - [validation] The normalised telephone must not match any **non-deleted** existing owner's telephone \u2192 else `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n7. **RequireUniqueHousehold** *(txn)*\n   - [validation] Unless the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, and only when a postcode is present, the derived `HouseholdId` (normalised lastName + postcode) must not collide with any **non-deleted** owner \u2192 else `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n8. **RequireCityCapacity** *(txn)*\n   - [validation] The city must hold fewer than 50 owners \u2192 else `CityAtCapacityException`. (Note: this count does **not** exclude soft-deleted owners, unlike steps 6 and 7.)\n\n9. **RequireDailyCapacity** *(txn)*\n   - [validation] Fewer than 100 owners may already carry the request's registration date (business-day-rolled; defaults to today) \u2192 else `DailyLimitException`.\n\n10. **BuildOwner** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity (id and pets ignored).\n    - [side-effect] Sets `registrationDate = BusinessDay.roll(supplied date or today)` \u2014 a weekend or listed public holiday rolls forward to the next business day.\n\n11. **AssignCustomerCode** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`: region derived from the postcode/city (`Locality`), and HASH8 = first 8 uppercase hex chars of SHA-256 over `E164(telephone) + lastName`.\n\n12. **DeduplicateCustomerCode** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] If that code already exists on another owner, appends `-<n>` using the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n13. **CountNamesakes** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same `HouseholdId` (feeds the membership tier). (Counts all existing owners, including soft-deleted.)\n\n14. **DetectPossibleDuplicate** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Unless `sharesHousehold=true` and only when a postcode is present, sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the id of an existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone (a soft/suspected duplicate).\n\n15. **SaveOwner** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n    - [side-effect] Writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, computed membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n16. **RecordIdempotency** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] If the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner id` (`putIfAbsent`) so a later identical create replays this owner.\n\n17. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(txn)*\n    - [side-effect] Maps the owner to `OwnerDto`, computing derived response fields via the mapper: `telephoneDisplay`, `displayName`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `checkDigit`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `possibleDuplicate`, `salutation`.\n    - [side-effect] Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = `BulkSignup.warningToday` (true once more than 80 owners have been created today).\n    - [side-effect] Responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the DTO body.\n    - The governed transaction commits at pipeline end.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- The **transaction only spans steps 6\u201317** (`identity` onward). Steps 1\u20135 \u2014 including all input validation, address normalisation, and email/telephone normalisation \u2014 run *outside* any transaction.\n- Two \"uniqueness/count\" checks are **inconsistent about soft-deleted owners**: `RequireUniqueIdentity` and `RequireUniqueHousehold` skip `isDeleted()` owners, but `RequireCityCapacity` (step 8) and `CountNamesakes` (step 13) count them. I'm surfacing this as an observation, not changing anything."
